      "text": "Let's solve this step by step:\n\n1. **Determine the Radius of the Semicircles:**\n   - Each arc \\(ADB\\) and \\(BEC\\) is a semicircle with a radius of 1 unit.\n   - Length of \\(AB\\) (which is equivalent to the diameter of arc \\(ADB\\)) can be calculated using the Pythagorean theorem:\n     \\[\n     AB = \\sqrt{r^2 + r^2} = \\sqrt{2} \\text{ units}\n     \\]\n   - Similarly, for arc \\(BEC\\), the diameter (length of \\(BE\\)) is also \\(\\sqrt{2}\\) units.\n\n2. **Calculate the Areas of the Semicircles:**\n   - The area of a semicircle is given by the formula \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\pi r^2 \\).\n   - The area of semicircle \\(ADB\\) is:\n     \\[\n     A_{ADB} = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi (1)^2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi \\text{ square units}\n     \\]\n   - The area of semicircle \\(BEC\\) is:\n     \\[\n     A_{BEC} = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi (1)^2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi \\text{ square units}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the Area of the Quarter Circle \\(DFE\\):**\n   - Since \\(D\\), \\(E\\), and \\(F\\) are the midpoints of the arcs \\(ADB\\), \\(BEC\\), and \\(DFE\\) respectively, the semicircle \\(DFE\\) will have half the radius of the semicircle \\(ADB\\).\n   - Therefore, the radius of \\(DFE\\) is 0.5 units (since it is the midpoint).\n   - The area of semicircle \\(DFE\\) is:\n     \\[\n     A_{DFE} = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi (0.5)^2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi \\times 0.25 = \\frac{1}{20} \\pi \\text{ square units}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Find the Area of the Unshaded Triangle \\(ABD\\):**\n   - Triangle \\(ABD\\) can be decomposed into two right triangles, \\( \\triangle ABD \\) and \\( \\triangle ABB \\).\n   - The area of \\( \\triangle ABD \\) is calculated as:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Area of } \\triangle ABD = \\frac{1}{2} \\times AB \\times r = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\sqrt{2} \\times 1 = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\text{ square units}\n     \\]\n   - Similarly, the area of \\( \\triangle ABB \\) is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Area of } \\triangle ABB = \\frac{1}{2} \\times AB \\times r = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\sqrt{2} \\times 1 = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\text{ square units}\n     \\]\n   - Therefore, the total area of \\( \\triangle ABD \\) is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Area of } \\triangle ABD = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} = \\sqrt{2} \\text{ square units}\n     \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the Total Shaded Area:**\n   - The shaded region is the area between the two arcs minus the area of the quarter circle plus the unshaded triangle.\n   - Thus, the area of the shaded region is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Total Shaded Area} = \\left(-\\frac{1}{2} \\pi + \\frac{1}{2} \\pi \\right) - \\left(0 - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\right) = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} = \\sqrt{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the shaded regions is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]",
