      "text": "To find the area of the shaded region, we need to calculate the area of the entire circle and subtract the areas of the unshaded regions within it.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the area of the entire circle. The circle has a radius of 1 unit, so the area is given by:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\pi \\times (\\text{radius})^2 = \\pi \\times 1^2 = \\pi \\]\n\nNext, we need to calculate the area of the unshaded regions. The unshaded regions are the areas of the sectors of the semicircles that lie outside the shaded region.\n\nSince each semicircle has a radius of 1 unit, the area of each semicircle is:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area of semicircle} = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi \\times 1^2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi \\]\n\nThere are three such semicircles (ADB, BEC, and DFE), so the total area of the semicircles is:\n\n\\[ 3 \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\pi = \\frac{3}{2} \\pi \\]\n\nHowever, we are told that arc DFE is also a semicircle, and it is given that the shaded region is composed of the area of three semicircles minus the area of a smaller semicircle. The area of the smaller semicircle is:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area of smaller semicircle} = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi \\]\n\nSo, the unshaded region consists of the area of three semicircles minus the area of the smaller semicircle:\n\n\\[ 3 \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\pi - \\frac{1}{2} \\pi = 2 \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\pi = \\pi \\]\n\nThus, the area of the unshaded regions is \\(\\pi\\).\n\nFinally, the area of the shaded region is the area of the entire circle minus the area of the unshaded regions:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area of shaded region} = \\pi - \\pi = 0 \\]\n\nSince we are asked to box the answer, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{0}\n\\]",
